  (text "Commander front battery bar (rev S0) - BMS board, microcontroller and the ports.\n\nSTC8H8K64U (the keyboard's and the internal battery's chip: one part number, one tool chain), at 3.3 V.  It is the\nbar's gauge and charge controller, and a USB HID 'Power Device' (UPS class) towards the terminal, exactly like the\ninternal battery module (commander_battery), so the terminal's software sees either of them the same way.\n\nTwo ports, wired in parallel (only one is used at a time):\nJ1  USB-C receptacle on the bar's left end face: charge the bar from any USB charger, use it as a power bank, or\ncable it to the terminal's battery port J40;\nJ4  the dock: a 5-way harness to the bar's docking contacts (INPUT_MODULE_CONNECTOR of the chassis model), so the\nbar powers the terminal when it is clipped on, without a cable.\nThe port role is the internal module's: Rp (36 k to 3.3 V) by default = 'I am a source'; Rd switched in when the\nterminal asks for a charge (HID feature report).  See README.md." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 25.4 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left top)) (uuid "1d4effbf-fd59-5bbd-9bd3-2293a3f55c14"))
